Android POTA Chase consumes the public Parks on the Air activator-spot API and
worldwide park catalogue from api.pota.app and pota.app. POTA names and park
data remain attributable to Parks on the Air. RigWeave is an independent
application and does not imply official hunter credit, affiliation, or
authoritative park boundaries.

Android POTA Activate uses the downloaded catalogue and official POTA rules to
prepare local ADIF files. Spotting and log submission are operator-controlled
browser handoffs to pota.app; RigWeave uses no POTA write API or credentials.

Android Portable Chase consumes the WWFF Spotline public integration spot and
active-agenda JSON feeds from spots.wwff.co and the official downloadable SOTA
summit list from sotadata.org.uk. WWFF and SOTA names and data remain
attributable to their respective programmes. The full WWFF Directory is not
stored without permission. SOTA live access is disabled pending approval under
the current private-API terms; no deprecated or unauthorized endpoint is used.

The Android Home operating dashboard is a native RigWeave integration inspired
by OpenHamClock (https://github.com/accius/openhamclock), inspected at immutable
commit d4a50eaaa61d3432a1de5f80cbe61790739930a5. OpenHamClock is distributed
under the MIT License, Copyright 2024-2026 OpenHamClock Contributors. RigWeave
does not embed its React/Express application, source files, artwork, server,
deployment controls, or runtime dependencies. The native Compose implementation
reuses RigWeave data controllers and design language. See
docs/OPENHAMCLOCK_INTEGRATION.md for the recorded integration boundary.

The Neural DX workspace uses F1SMV/Neural-DX-Watcher
(https://github.com/F1SMV/Neural-DX-Watcher) as a behavioural reference. The
approved upstream v12.1 behavioural baseline is
fe3cba8ed9c0502f5dabdb2f64ebd990de986559. The original remediation brief
contained a non-resolving transcription/reference error. No upstream licence or
permission grant was found, and no upstream source or assets are bundled by this
